.TH SIGMA_DIFFERENCE 1 2000-1月 "genome.gc_skew" "genome.gc_skew"
.SH NAME
genome.gc_skew \- The \fB(C - G) / (C + G)\fR sliding window profile of the genome strand
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIgenome.gc_skew(\fBgenome\fR as <generic> FastaSeq, 
\fBwindowSize\fR as integer = 10000, 
\fBstepSize\fR as integer = 1000);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fB(C - G) / (C + G)\fR sliding window profile of the genome strand
 composition asymmetry: the leading strand favors purines (G > C), so the
 curve flips its sign at the replication origin oriC.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBgenome\fB \fR\- the genome nucleotide sequence. 
.PP
.PP
\fBwindowSize\fB \fR\- the sliding window size in bp, default 10kb. 
.PP
.PP
\fBstepSize\fB \fR\- the sampling step in bp, default 1kb. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the skew profile rows ordered by the site position
.PP
